# Source: Ventrax AV4 report. Acceptance specification; execution is verified separately.
Feature: API routing and perimeter security

  Scenario: Route an authorized request to a backend service
    Given an authenticated client provides a valid JWT
    When the client requests a configured protected route
    Then the Gateway forwards the request to the corresponding local backend service

  Scenario: Reject an invalid or expired JWT
    Given a client provides an invalid or expired access token
    When the client requests a protected route
    Then the Gateway rejects the request with the appropriate authentication error

  Scenario: Preserve resource-level authorization
    Given a subuser has a valid JWT but lacks permission for meter B
    When the subuser requests a protected operation for meter B
    Then the backend denies the operation according to its current resource permissions

  Scenario: Handle an unavailable backend
    Given a configured backend service is unavailable
    When the Gateway attempts to route a request to that service
    Then the Gateway returns a controlled error without exposing internal credentials
